# benzylamine.msf
# Benzylamine (phenylmethylamine)
# pKa=9.340 (PhCH2NH3+ → PhCH2NH2, q=+1→0)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# Benzylic amine: sp3 nitrogen but adjacent to aromatic ring via CH2.
# pKa sits between aliphatic amines (~10.5) and aromatic amines (~4-5),
# testing whether the model interpolates correctly through the CH2 spacer.
# Useful benchmark for drug-like amines (many drugs have benzylic N).

